{"name":"Thyme and Place","hex":"#6f8770","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"thyme","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the labiate genus Thymus, such as garden thyme (Thymus vulgaris), a warm, pungent aromatic, that is much used to give a relish to seasoning and soups."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thyme"},{"term":"and","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ansus."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.\nUsed simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\nSimply connecting two clauses or sentences. \n\nIntroducing a clause or sentence which follows on in time or consequence from the first.","Used simply to connect two noun phrases, adjectives or adverbs. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/and"},{"term":"place","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area; somewhere within an area.\nAn open space, particularly a city square, market square, or courtyard.\n\n A street, sometimes but not always surrounding a public place, square, or plaza of the same name.","An open space, particularly a city square, market square, or courtyard."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put (someone or something) in a specific location.","To earn a given spot in a competition; to rank at a certain position ()."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/place"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thyme","blocks":[{"text":"Thyme is a culinary herb consisting of the dried aerial parts of some members of the genus Thymus of flowering plants in the mint family Lamiaceae. Thymes are native to Mediterranean countries in North Africa, Levant and Southern Europe. Thymes have culinary, medicinal, and ornamental uses. The species most commonly cultivated and used for culinary purposes is Thymus vulgaris, native to Southeast Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Thyme-Bundle.jpg/330px-Thyme-Bundle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thyme"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Flowering_thyme.JPG/500px-Flowering_thyme.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Flowering_thyme.JPG/1280px-Flowering_thyme.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Flowering_thyme.JPG/500px-Flowering_thyme.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flowering thyme","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlowering_thyme.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Seombaengnihyang-cha.jpg/500px-Seombaengnihyang-cha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Seombaengnihyang-cha.jpg/1280px-Seombaengnihyang-cha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Seombaengnihyang-cha.jpg/500px-Seombaengnihyang-cha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Seombaengnihyang-cha (Ulleungdo thyme tea)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeombaengnihyang-cha.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Variegated_Lemon_Thyme_Thymus_citriodorus_variegata_Leaves_3264px.JPG/500px-Variegated_Lemon_Thyme_Thymus_citriodorus_variegata_Leaves_3264px.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Variegated_Lemon_Thy